    <string-array name="tip_home">
        <item>This is your house</item>
        <item>Rooms light up as you write down what’s in them; empty ones stay dark corners.</item>
        <item>The hob’s notes are on top: what’s needed soon, what’s lent, what a child has grown into.</item>
        <item>Tap the search to ask where something is.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_find">
        <item>Ask the hob</item>
        <item>Type a word: a name, a room, the label on a box.</item>
        <item>Tap a kind below to see all the tools or all the papers.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_people">
        <item>Who has what</item>
        <item>Lend a thing from its card – the hob reminds you when to ask for it back.</item>
        <item>Add the children with their height and shoe size: the hob will say when the things on the shelves fit.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_hob">
        <item>Meet the hob</item>
        <item>He likes lit rooms, clean shelves and things that come back.</item>
        <item>Cosiness grows from all of it; with it his title grows from guest to old-timer.</item>
        <item>After a clear-out, leave him some milk.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_room">
        <item>A room</item>
        <item>Things lie in places: the top shelf, under the bed. Add your own places at the bottom.</item>
        <item>Boxes have numbers – write the number on the box itself.</item>
        <item>«+ here» writes a new thing straight into this place.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_thing">
        <item>A thing’s card</item>
        <item>«Used it» tells the hob the thing is alive – otherwise in a year he’ll ask if it’s still needed.</item>
        <item>Lend it, move it, or let it go: give away, sell or throw out.</item>
        <item>The history keeps who wore it and who borrowed it.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_add">
        <item>Write a thing down</item>
        <item>A name is enough: the sign and the kind come from it.</item>
        <item>Choose the room and the place; a box if it’s in one.</item>
        <item>For children’s clothes, enter the size from the label – the hob will count when it fits.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_clear">
        <item>A clear-out</item>
        <item>Things untouched for a year come one by one.</item>
        <item>Keep, give away, sell or throw out – one tap each.</item>
        <item>In doubt, keep it: the hob asks again next year.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="tip_kid">
        <item>A child</item>
        <item>Measure every few months: the forecast follows their own pace.</item>
        <item>Below are the things waiting on the shelves, with when each will fit.</item>
    </string-array>
